{"answer":null,"concept_id":"atomics-cost-determinism","content_sha256":"sha256:0b98b9c8388427a50ed53134469bc51fec28d710a8031cbd3944f6130e41c258","correct_option_ids":["a"],"created_at":1789332404.291987,"domain":"operator-development","explanation":"原子性解决的是竞争正确性；同一地址的原子操作会串行化，高频冲突让 kernel 退化。float atomicAdd 因浮点加法非结合性，完成顺序不同则结果每次不同——这不是 bug 而是数值特性；需要确定性时用树形归约、分桶合并或固定顺序。","id":"q-operator-atomics-cost-determinism-001","options":[{"id":"a","text":"原子读改写保证竞争下的正确性（直方图、计数），但热点地址会硬件串行化、性能受损；浮点 atomics 完成顺序不定导致结果不可复现，要确定性需改归约/固定顺序方案"},{"id":"b","text":"atomics 没有性能代价，可以大量使用"},{"id":"c","text":"atomics 能保证浮点求和的位级可复现"},{"id":"d","text":"atomics 只能用于整数类型"}],"prompt":"CUDA atomic 操作的正确性收益与代价分别是什么？","schema_version":"question/v1","skill":"tradeoff","source_refs":[{"kind":"official_docs","title":"NVIDIA CUDA C++ Programming Guide","url":"https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/cuda-c-programming-guide/"},{"kind":"public_interview_topic","title":"NVIDIA CUDA interview topics","url":"https://huru.ai/nvidia-interview-questions-mastering-cuda-inference-systems"}],"status":"enabled","topic":"sync","type":"single_choice","wiki_refs":[]}
